# Ticket Status Hygiene

When work satisfies a ticket's acceptance criteria, update that ticket's frontmatter `status` before considering the work complete.

Use the ticket file as the source of truth:

- Read `depends_on`, `status`, `domain`, and the full Acceptance criteria section before implementation.
- Do not mark a ticket done if any AC remains unmet or unverified.
- If implementation is complete but verification is pending, leave `status` as `backlog` or move to the project-standard intermediate status only if one exists in roadmap conventions.
- If all AC are met and verified, update `status` to `done` in the relevant `docs/Roadmap/tickets/CS-*.md` file.
- If a ticket becomes blocked or needs a follow-up split, record that in the ticket or PR notes instead of silently leaving stale status.
- Phase index files are navigation only; never treat them as the authoritative status location.

